WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.620
With Season 5B of Lucifer here, it's time
to hunt through all the new episodes for those

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.920
delicious easter eggs and hilarious details
the crew snuck in for all us Lucifans!

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.670
"So many easter eggs from our previous adventures."

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.680
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the top 50 heavenly

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.850
details you missed in Part 2 of Lucifer Season
5!

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.830
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.130
Lucifer proves he's a devil of his word at
the start of episode 9.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.660
See this guy dancing at Lux as Luci plays
"Footloose" on the piano?

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.560
Well, he's the security guard that Luci made
a devilish deal with in the midseason finale:

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.630
"I want to be a dancer."

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.420
"Well, you're in luck, Baryshnikov.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.530
I'll hire you and make your Footloose dreams
come true.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.530
What do you say?

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.530
Deal?"

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.829
Given Dan's previous relationship with the
Goddess, meeting her husband was always going

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:47.829
to be super-awkward.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:51.780
So, I bet he was glad to see Lucifer distract
God with some snacks:

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.690
"Dad, why don't I show you the vending machines?

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.990
Have you tried Cool Ranch Puffs?"

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:59.510
And as we know from Season 1, those particular
snacks are Luci's favourites:

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:00.510
"Cool ranch puff?

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:01.610
It's funny, isn't it?

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.170
You'd think the king of hellfire would be
more of a flaming hot guy, but..."

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.970
I love the symmetry of these shots of Lucifer
and God when they end up in a therapy session

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:13.330
at Dr Linda's as it shows that father and
son have more in common than they might think,

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:17.050
pointing to how Lucifer will become God in
the season finale.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:21.500
And if you look carefully, you can see a parenting
book called How To Raise Successful People

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.530
on Linda's desk, which she's doubtless reading
for her son Charlie,

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:29.840
but it also feels fitting for the high-powered
people currently occupying her couch.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.979
The musical episode is an absolute blast,
with lively performances, Busby Berkeley-style

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:38.100
choreography, a cameo from singer-songwriter
Debbie Gibson;

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:41.150
and yes, even God starts bopping along.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.780
On top of that, we also get plenty of signs
of what's to come by the end of the season:

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.170
Dan's concerns over having slept with God's
wife,

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.439
"Which means I'm definitely going to Hell"
and the song he sings foreshadow Amenadiel's

00:01:52.439 --> 00:01:55.619
discovery that his friend isn't in Heaven.

00:01:55.619 --> 00:01:59.759
Lucifer shutting down a flame with his hand
and his clothes burning up while he remains

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:00.909
unscathed,
"You okay?"

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:01.909
"Yes.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:02.909
Of course I am."

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:08.090
foreshadow his flaming fate in Heaven and
signal that ultimately he'll emerge unharmed.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:12.340
And then there are the literal signs we see
Chloe and Lucifer standing by at the school

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.939
as she tells him she has faith in him and
that she's sure he'll work things out with

00:02:15.939 --> 00:02:16.939
his dad.

00:02:16.939 --> 00:02:21.900
'Flying to the top in just one day' and 'Another
victory on its way', say the signs, pointing

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.900
to Chloe and Luci's heavenly ascent in the
finale and Team Lucifer's triumph over his

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.560
villainous twin.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.010
At the gym of self-styled "fitness guru to
the stars", Kristoff, there's a bunch of posters

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.260
of well-known clients he's worked with, all
of whom have been part of Chloe and Luci's

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.269
cases at some point.

00:02:38.269 --> 00:02:42.519
There's the cast of ¡Lieutenant Diablo!,
the network TV show that's an hilariously

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:43.959
OTT version of Lucifer.

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:49.309
And there's Holla Bae, a murdered DJ whose
body was taken over by a demon in the season

00:02:49.309 --> 00:02:50.309
4 finale.

00:02:50.309 --> 00:02:55.219
Then there's the Blazing Banshees, a roller
derby team involved in a murder-kidnap case,

00:02:55.219 --> 00:02:57.420
and their rivals the Derby Divas.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:01.590
The Bobby Lowe Show features a comedian who
stole jokes from another comic that ended

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.559
up being murdered before he could reveal the
truth.

00:03:04.559 --> 00:03:09.549
Axara is the pop sensation whose life was
threatened in the episode Let Pinhead Sing!

00:03:09.549 --> 00:03:14.199
As for Top Meet, that's an exclusive celebrity
dating app whose designer was murdered.

00:03:14.199 --> 00:03:19.120
And apparently, Kristoff has featured on "The
Cabin", a hit reality TV programme Ella loves

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.599
where a contestant was killed in Season 4.

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:26.180
Given so many of the clients in the posters
are now dead, it certainly brings new meaning

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.040
to the sign "Bodies by Kristoff".

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.699
When Lucifer and Chloe go to interview a murder
suspect who owns an adventure park, he gets

00:03:33.699 --> 00:03:37.209
the wrong end of the stick and tries to flee
the scene in one of his go-karts:

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:39.290
"Thought you were arresting me for the ZX3!

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:42.150
It's an illegal..."
"...chemical used in street racing.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.739
Surprisingly useful in other ways.

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:44.739
We're familiar."

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:48.809
This is a throwback to Season 2 where Luci
went to hell and back to get the formula for

00:03:48.809 --> 00:03:51.849
the antidote to save Chloe after she was poisoned.

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:55.489
And ZX3 was the final ingredient needed to
create that antidote.

00:03:55.489 --> 00:03:56.840
"A chemical called ZX3.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.180
Super rare, super illegal."

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:03.439
In a somewhat ironic twist, the same chemical
that was used to save a life back then winds

00:04:03.439 --> 00:04:05.260
up ending one this season.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.589
"We found traces of ZX3 in the fuel that burned
down the Kingdom."

00:04:08.589 --> 00:04:13.209
Most crucially though, the fact this super-rare
chemical crops up again at the start of Season

00:04:13.209 --> 00:04:18.280
5B foreshadows how Chloe will need saving
from death once more in the season finale.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:23.140
In an effort to work on his relationship with
his father, Lucifer takes him to the precinct,

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:28.060
but God's reaction when he discovers Luci
doesn't have a throne, office, or even a desk

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.480
is priceless, and Dennis Haysbert delivers
the line perfectly:

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.480
"He has a desk.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.130
Maybe if you work hard enough, you might one
day rise to this man's level."

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:42.290
This comment must really sting as Lucifer's
not only being compared unfavourably to Detective

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:47.011
Douche, but it'll probably also remind him
of how Chloe turned him down in Season 2 when

00:04:47.011 --> 00:04:49.140
he requested a desk next to hers.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.070
"I should get my own desk."

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.070
"Not happening."

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.140
"Right next to yours would probably be best."

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.140
"Definitely not happening."

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:59.070
Of course, their relationship was at a very
different stage to that by Season 5A and Lucifer

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.860
was happy to see Chloe make herself at home
at his desk in Lux:

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.670
"This desk has never looked so good."

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:09.030
When Team Lucifer try stalling their face-off
with Michael to give Maze time to arrive,

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.730
they break into song to pretend that God's
back.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:16.230
But this isn't the first time that MC Hammer's
U Can't Touch has cropped up on the show.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:20.540
In Season 4, during their investigation into
the death of a realtor, Ella also broke out

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.040
the 90s track.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.040
"Stop!

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.310
Hammer time!"

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:30.500
In the midst of his insane adventures in episode
12, Dan tells Ella he needs some advice to

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.690
get inside the criminal mind:
"I actually do know how to fake the perfect

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:35.690
murder.

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.690
Because...

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.280
I've been working on it for my novel.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.430
So, it's about a forensic scientist who talks
to ghosts."

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:45.480
Ella first mentioned that book in Season 3
"I'm actually writing my own book about a

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:48.960
forensic scientist who talks to ghosts."
and it's based on her own friendship since

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.010
she was a child with a ghost named Rae-Rae.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:56.880
Continuing the ghostly theme, in another episode,
Ella wears a T-shirt with the pun Holy Sheet

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:01.750
on it that features a ghost wearing a halo,
which is perfect because that ghost Ella believes

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:06.590
she met as a kid is actually a holy being:
Lucifer's sister, Azrael!

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:11.280
In episode 11, as a doctor gets ready to perform
her latest surgery, she says:

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.820
It's a beautiful day to operate.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:16.900
Which is a play on the line "It's a beautiful
day to save lives" from the long-running medical

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.840
drama Grey's Anatomy.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:22.710
When Lucifer arrives at an aquarium where
a body's been dumped in the shark tank, the

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:26.770
first thing he says is:
"Sharks, one of Earth's most misunderstood

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:27.770
creatures.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:29.800
Definitely correcting that when I'm God."

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:33.720
Which is a throw-back to Season 3 where he
decided there were better ways to spend his

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:38.400
time than trying to kill Pierce, aka Cain:
"There are far better ways to spend my time."

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.400
"Oh?"

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.400
"Take a nude painting class.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.430
Buy that pet shark I've always wanted."

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:47.520
The number on the ticket Luci gets when he
leaves his car with a valet is 666, the number

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:52.310
of the beast in the Book of Revelation and
widely associated with the Antichrist or devil.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.920
This isn't the first time that number's appeared,
for example, it was also tattooed on Lucifer's

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:57.920
torso.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:01.840
And when Luci appeared during an Arrowverse
crossover event, we learnt that he lives on

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.940
Earth-666.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:08.550
When God pops up at a crime scene and tells
Chloe he's made himself human, Lucifer makes

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:11.830
a joke of it:
"Oh, he does inexplicable things from time

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:12.830
to time.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.920
Marsupials, pomegranates, the gall bladder."

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:19.100
As throwaway as that gag is, the mention of
pomegranates caught my attention as they've

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:23.110
appeared on the show before, with several
paintings of them in the law office of Charlotte

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.150
the Goddess.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:28.350
Which is fitting as some scholars believe
that pomegranates, not apples, were the fruit

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:31.640
that tempted Adam and Eve in the Garden of
Eden.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.621
When Chloe asks a medium where she was during
a murder, she replies:

00:07:34.621 --> 00:07:38.580
"Giving a reading...
to a programming exec...

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:39.580
at Fox."

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:40.880
"Oh, good luck with that."

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:45.050
Lucifer's comment is a hilarious burn on the
show's previous home Fox which cancelled the

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:50.090
series after its third season, following which
an online campaign by Lucifans saw it picked

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:51.880
up by Netflix.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:56.250
As Amenadiel excitedly reveals he wants to
join the police and would love to work with

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.500
Dan one day, his friend's response isn't anywhere
near as supportive as he'd hoped:

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:03.970
"Yeah, an angel and a detective solving crimes,
makes total sense."

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:08.240
Of course, we love meta-moments like this
one in the series, which basically sums up

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:11.290
the premise of the show, and is a spin on
Luci's song:

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.430
"Crime-solving Devil.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.140
It makes sense.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.420
Don't over think it."

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:21.010
During Lucifer's mission to find out which
of his siblings will help him rather than

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.210
Michael become God, he says to his brother
Jophiel:

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:27.650
"I'm assuming you're Team Lucifer"
Which is a call-back to the Season 1 episode

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:33.370
#TeamLucifer where corrupt cop Malcolm told
Amenadiel he wasn't going to help him kill

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.149
Luci anymore:
"Unless you got a better offer...

00:08:35.149 --> 00:08:36.149
#TeamLucifer."

00:08:36.149 --> 00:08:37.149
Also, I love the writers' sense of humour
in making Jophiel a huge himbo as, according

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:38.149
to Wikipedia, not only does his name mean
"divine beauty" but he's also supposed to

00:08:38.149 --> 00:08:39.149
be an "archangel of wisdom, understanding,
and judgment".

00:08:39.149 --> 00:08:43.259
The day Season 5A dropped on Netflix, Tom
Ellis was straight on social media tweeting

00:08:43.259 --> 00:08:44.259
#michaelisadick.

00:08:44.259 --> 00:08:50.180
And a shout-out to that trending topic made
it into Season 5B when Jophiel and Lucifer

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:54.510
discuss Michael's nefarious ways:
"Whispering in Dad's ear, making him think

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:58.500
he was losing his powers in the first place,
all so he could take over now."

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.709
"Yeah, Michael's kind of a dick."

00:08:59.709 --> 00:09:01.209
He's a massive dick.

00:09:01.209 --> 00:09:05.850
At the start of the season finale, Michael
plays an off-key version of the popular jazz

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:11.029
song Heart And Soul, which is often performed
as a piano duet, as it was by Chloe and Lucifer

00:09:11.029 --> 00:09:12.610
in Season 1.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:16.889
Michael's out-of-tune performance and the
fact he plays by himself fits perfectly with

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:21.459
his whole character and emphasises how totally
at odds he is in everything with his musical

00:09:21.459 --> 00:09:23.199
and sociable twin brother.

00:09:23.199 --> 00:09:27.740
Also, intriguingly, two of the times this
particular song has popped up in the series,

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.660
it's happened shortly before a reveal that
one of Luci's brothers has got their hands

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:35.819
on a weapon that could have dire consequences
for the devil and even the world.

00:09:35.819 --> 00:09:40.910
In season 1, it was an untraceable gun that
Amenadiel wanted Malcolm to kill Lucifer with.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:45.019
While in season 5B, it's the Flaming Sword,
which Michael claims to have, though he's

00:09:45.019 --> 00:09:49.630
lying at that point, and which he intends
to use to beat Lucifer in the latest Celestial

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:50.709
battle.

00:09:50.709 --> 00:09:54.881
When God and the Goddess finally exit this
world to live together in her universe, they

00:09:54.881 --> 00:09:59.449
do so at Lucifer's club, pulling aside the
curtains and walking out into the light.

00:09:59.449 --> 00:10:04.800
All of which happens, appropriately enough,
right underneath the sign LUX, the Latin word

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:05.829
for light!

00:10:05.829 --> 00:10:08.310
Lucifer decides to pick up a new instrument
this season:

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:09.869
"I think I'm going to learn the French horn."

00:10:09.869 --> 00:10:14.310
Which is a fun hat-tip to Tom Ellis's own
life as he actually learned to play the French

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:18.980
horn at the age of 8 or 9 and played in orchestras,
including the City of Sheffield Youth Orchestra,

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:20.399
throughout his teenage years.

00:10:20.399 --> 00:10:21.399
"My French horn.

00:10:21.399 --> 00:10:22.779
Just on my way to chuck it out."

00:10:22.779 --> 00:10:26.709
While Eve waits for her date to turn up at
the bar, she drinks an appletini, the same

00:10:26.709 --> 00:10:29.540
tipple she ordered when she first appeared
in Season 4,

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:33.649
though this time it comes complete with a
slice of apple, all of which is a nice nod

00:10:33.649 --> 00:10:38.690
to Eve's backstory with what's often thought
to be the Garden of Eden's forbidden fruit.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:41.829
Just when Michael thinks Lucifer has accepted
him as the new God,

00:10:41.829 --> 00:10:43.619
"You ready to bend the knee, brother?"

00:10:43.619 --> 00:10:48.329
his devilish twin pulls a fast one:
"You are God...

00:10:48.329 --> 00:10:49.329
awful!

00:10:49.329 --> 00:10:52.509
What on earth are you wearing?

00:10:52.509 --> 00:10:54.059
Is winter coming or something?"

00:10:54.059 --> 00:10:58.139
But Lucifer trash-talking his brother's Game
of Thrones-style garb isn't the first time

00:10:58.139 --> 00:11:00.660
he's used the hit show's famous phrase.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:04.360
Back when Chloe was worried about Father Kinley's
prophecy, Luci asked her:

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.379
"What is it this time?

00:11:05.379 --> 00:11:06.480
Perhaps winter is coming."

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:11.149
And, I'm not sure if it's intended but, at
the family dinner, when Lucifer noisily drags

00:11:11.149 --> 00:11:15.520
his chair to the head of the table, I couldn't
help but think of a certain Thrones character

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:27.529
who also had a rather difficult relationship
with his family.

00:11:27.529 --> 00:11:32.100
When Chloe reunites with her dad in Heaven,
they enjoy a picnic together and, in a lovely

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:36.740
throwback to season 2, the traditional Decker
family egg sandwiches are on the menu:

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:37.740
"Egg sandwiches.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:39.250
A Decker family tradition."

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.250
[Chloe] So good.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:43.949
"Grandpa used to bring me this sandwich every
Thursday after acting class."

00:11:43.949 --> 00:11:44.959
"So good."

00:11:44.959 --> 00:11:49.839
By the way, the actor who plays Chloe's father
here is Chris Payne Gilbert, real-life husband

00:11:49.839 --> 00:11:52.119
of Maze actress Lesley-Ann Brandt.

00:11:52.119 --> 00:11:57.440
Lucifer is met in Heaven by Lee, aka Mr Said-Out
Bitch, who's been a regular in the show's

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.600
season premieres over the years.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:03.360
And when Luci says he's been saved by Lilith's
immortality ring, Lee's reply:

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.839
"I don't know what the fork any of that means."

00:12:05.839 --> 00:12:10.170
is a tribute to the brilliant TV comedy The
Good Place set in the afterlife where curse

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:12.279
words are censored in hilarious ways.

00:12:12.279 --> 00:12:13.709
"Somebody royally forked up.

00:12:13.709 --> 00:12:15.490
Why can't I say 'fork'?"

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:19.879
Maze breaks down when she finds an old T-shirt
Dan had to pinch after she knocked him out

00:12:19.879 --> 00:12:22.899
and left him naked in Chloe's bed back in
Season 1.

00:12:22.899 --> 00:12:28.249
That NSYNC T-shirt, which originally belonged
to Chloe, reflects her love of 90s music,

00:12:28.249 --> 00:12:30.869
something Lucifer has ribbed her about over
the years:

00:12:30.869 --> 00:12:32.790
"Full of '90s jams, I see.

